    },
    {
     "type": "note",
     "title": "Upside-down verbs",
     "md": "With these four verbs, the **thing** is the subject and the **person** is in the **Dativ**:\n\n- {de:**Das Bild** gefällt **mir**.} = *the picture pleases me* → I like the picture.\n- {de:**Das Brot** schmeckt **mir**.} → I like the bread (taste).\n- {de:**Die Jacke** passt **dir**.} → the jacket fits you.\n- {de:**Das Handy** gehört **mir**.} → the phone is mine.\n\nThe verb follows the **thing**: one thing → *gefällt*, several → *gefallen*: {de:Die Farben gefallen ihnen.}\n\nDativ pronouns: **mir, dir, ihm, ihr, uns, euch, ihnen / Ihnen**."
    },
    {
